n the last leaves. `orders.delivery_fee_refunded` tracks partial refunds so a residual base stuck on an already-cancelled base row is returned (across sibling payments) when the last farmer finally leaves. `src/lib/delivery-refund.ts` issues the sibling-payment refunds. Legacy null-checkout_id orders keep old per-order behavior.\n\nImportant change: delivery fee is now **charged online** (added to Razorpay create amount; COD deposit already folded it via computeCodSplit) so it's refundable — previously it was `DELIVERY_FEE_RUPEES=0` collected as cash by the rider. That constant is **removed**.\n\nFiles: `scripts/delivery-charge-migration.sql` (platform_settings.delivery_base_fee/delivery_extra_fee + orders.checkout_id + orders.delivery_fee_refunded — run in BOTH prod & staging), `src/lib/delivery-fee.ts`, `src/lib/delivery-refund.ts`, `src/app/api/moderator/delivery-fee/route.ts` + DeliveryChargeCard on `/moderator`, place/razorpay-create/decline/cancel routes, Cart + consumer order-detail display. No moderator order-decline route exists, so moderator parity = the config card only.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ffb75223-53ec-4b64-9d57-e29899e4d537","session_id":"b6577fe7-68cf-4607-bdd4-71d04060cfcc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/veerendra/farmer/yourfamilyfarmer","sessionId":"b6577fe7-68cf-4607-bdd4-71d04060cfcc","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"staging"}
